y brace lies still on the table edge. He has just answered \"No, nothing,\" a little too flatly. Her eyes drop to the bowl, she takes one small breath, and then, quietly, almost as if thinking aloud, with clear natural Korean mouth movements fully visible, S1 says: <d>[Korean] 근데 왜 사고가 났지.</d> She speaks in her own plain, soft mid-range voice from <Audio 1>, low in volume and even, with no tremble. At 00:03.500, after the line, she slowly lifts her eyes to him and holds his gaze, still and waiting, a small tension along her jaw, until the end.\n\noverall_soundscape: Quiet apartment room tone at night, a very faint refrigerator hum, the faint touch of the metal spoon against the ceramic bowl. Only S1's voice is heard.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
